.TH FL-ARCHIVE 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-archive \- archive manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-archive\fR [\fIARCHIVE\fR]
.br
\fBfl-archive\fR \fB\-\-extract\-here\fR|\fB\-\-extract\-ask\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR...
.br
\fBfl-archive\fR \fB\-\-extract\-to\fR \fIDIR\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR...
.br
\fBfl-archive\fR \fB\-\-compress\fR \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Browses, extracts, creates and changes archives with \fBlibarchive\fR(3). It reads zip, 7z, tar
(uncompressed or with gzip, xz, zstd, bzip2, lzip, lzma), rar, iso, cpio, cab, lha, deb, rpm, jar
and single compressed files (\fIfile.txt.gz\fR); it creates and changes zip, 7z and tar archives.
.PP
The window lists the archive's folders and files with their size, type and date; double-click a
folder to open it (Backspace goes up) and a file to open a copy with its program. \fBExtract\fR
unpacks the selected items, or everything, into a folder you choose. \fBAdd Files\fR and \fBAdd
Folder\fR put files into the current folder of the archive (files dropped on the window too) and
\fBDelete\fR removes the selected items; the archive is rewritten in its format. With nothing open,
\fBNew\fR or dropping files creates a new archive.
.PP
Zip archives can be encrypted with a password (AES-256); fl-archive asks for the password of
encrypted archives. Entries with absolute paths or "../" are never extracted outside the target
folder. When a file exists already, fl-archive asks whether to replace or skip it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-extract\-here\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR...
Extract next to each archive: an archive with a single top-level folder (or a single file) is
extracted as is, otherwise into a new folder named after the archive.
.TP
\fB\-\-extract\-to\fR \fIDIR\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR...
Extract into \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-extract\-ask\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR...
Ask for the folder to extract into.
.TP
\fB\-\-compress\fR \fIFILE\fR...
Ask for a name, format, folder and optional password and create an archive of the files.
.PP
The file manager \fBfl-files\fR(1) offers these as Extract Here, Extract To and Compress in its
context menu.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+N new archive, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+E extract, Delete removes the selection, Enter opens the
selected item, Backspace goes up a folder, Ctrl+Q quits.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbsdtar\fR(1), \fBfl-files\fR(1)
